<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Futuris extends Elders offer.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Futuris extends Elders offer.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diversified industrial group Futuris Corp Ltd said on Monday it would extend by two weeks to September 30 the offer period for its takeover offer for pastoral group Elders Australia Ltd.</p>
<p>Futuris said it now held 81.03 percent of Elders.</p>
<p>Futuris and Elders originally proposed a merger, but the move was stymied by overseas investors General Oriental Investments Ltd and Marathon Asset Management, which hold a combined stake of around 15 percent in Elders and were critical of merging the pastoral and industrial businesses.  </p>
<p>Futuris is offering 10 of its shares for every nine Elders shares plus 23 cents per Elders share.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
